The curb this scene walks over, and the clip it tracks, are curb_000's geometry and its
take 000 from NVIDIA's GRAIL dataset
(https://huggingface.co/datasets/nvidia/PhysicalAI-Robotics-Locomanipulation-GRAIL, at
40e7957), from "GRAIL: Generating Humanoid Loco-Manipulation from 3D Assets and Video
Priors" (arXiv:2606.05160). The dataset card states:

    "Use of the released dataset is governed by the Creative Commons Attribution-
     NonCommercial 4.0 International License (CC BY-NC 4.0)."

that its procedurally generated curbs, slopes and stairs are "GRAIL-original outputs,
released under CC BY-NC 4.0", and that the license covers its motion trajectories.

Changed here: ORCS stages the curb as a terrain tile and the take as a clip; this scene
builds the tile into its model, and its command graph carries the clip's frames.

The license's terms are at

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode

It permits sharing and adapting for noncommercial purposes only, with credit.
